    {
      "title": "Views and Materialized Views",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Views and Materialized Views",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a View Is",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==view== = a saved `SELECT` with a name",
                "Stores **no data**; re-runs its query on every access",
                "Replacement must keep existing column names and order (PostgreSQL)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW v AS SELECT ...;",
                "DROP VIEW v;"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Materialized Views",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Stores the result ==physically==",
                "Goes **stale** until you refresh it",
                "`CONCURRENTLY` needs a ==unique index==, does not block reads"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW mv AS SELECT ...;",
                "REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW CONCURRENTLY mv;"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "View",
                "Materialized"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Data",
                  "always fresh",
                  "{red:stale}"
                ],
                [
                  "Read speed",
                  "slower",
                  "**fast**"
                ],
                [
                  "Index",
                  "no",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Gotchas",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`SELECT *` is expanded at creation: later base-table columns do not appear",
                "Simple views are updatable",
                "`GROUP BY`, `DISTINCT` or joins usually make a view read-only"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "String Functions",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "String Functions",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Clean, Measure, Join",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`UPPER`, `LOWER`, `TRIM` (plus `LTRIM`/`RTRIM`) clean text",
                "`LENGTH` counts ==characters== in PostgreSQL, **bytes** in some engines",
                "`CONCAT(a,b)` treats NULL as ==empty== in PostgreSQL and SQL Server; {red:MySQL returns NULL}",
                "`||` returns {red:NULL} if any operand is NULL"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "SELECT CONCAT('a', NULL) AS c,",
                "       'a' || NULL AS p;"
              ],
              "result": {
                "headers": [
                  "c",
                  "p"
                ],
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "a",
                    "NULL"
                  ]
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Slice and Search",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Function",
                "Result",
                "Note"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`SUBSTRING(s, 2, 3)`",
                  "3 chars from position 2",
                  "==1-indexed=="
                ],
                [
                  "`LEFT(s, n)`",
                  "first n chars",
                  "from the start"
                ],
                [
                  "`RIGHT(s, n)`",
                  "last n chars",
                  "from the end"
                ],
                [
                  "`REPLACE(s, a, b)`",
                  "every `a` becomes `b`",
                  "**all** matches"
                ],
                [
                  "`POSITION('x' IN s)`",
                  "where `x` starts",
                  "{red:0} if not found"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`INSTR(s, 'x')` is the same idea in other engines"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Index Traps",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`LIKE '%abc'` leading wildcard: no plain index",
                "`WHERE LOWER(col) = ...`: no plain index",
                "Fix: a ==functional index== on `LOWER(col)`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Substring positions start at ==1==, not 0. For NULLs, wrap values in `COALESCE`: MySQL's `CONCAT` returns NULL too."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Date and Time Functions",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Date and Time Functions",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Now and Date Parts",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`CURRENT_DATE` returns a ==date==",
                "`NOW()` / `CURRENT_TIMESTAMP` return a ==timestamp with time zone==",
                "Both are **fixed for the whole transaction**",
                "`EXTRACT(YEAR FROM ts)` pulls out one part",
                "`DATE_TRUNC('month', ts)` rounds down to the period start; use it for monthly `GROUP BY`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Date Arithmetic",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Expression",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`ts + INTERVAL '7 days'`",
                  "timestamp"
                ],
                [
                  "`date - date`",
                  "{green:integer} day count"
                ],
                [
                  "`timestamp - timestamp`",
                  "{purple:interval}"
                ],
                [
                  "`AGE(a, b)`",
                  "years / months / days"
                ],
                [
                  "MySQL `DATEDIFF(a, b)`",
                  "days between a and b"
                ],
                [
                  "MySQL `DATE_ADD(d, INTERVAL 1 DAY)`",
                  "d plus one day"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Filtering a Timestamp Range",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`BETWEEN` with an end date misses that day after ==midnight==",
                "Use a half-open range: start included, end excluded"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "WHERE ts >= '2026-01-01'",
                "  AND ts <  '2026-02-01'"
              ],
              "note": "all of January, nothing from February"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Filter timestamps with ==>= start AND < next period==, never `BETWEEN`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "CASE, COALESCE and NULLIF",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "CASE, COALESCE and NULLIF",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. CASE",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Searched CASE: ==first true== WHEN wins",
                "No `ELSE` returns ==NULL==",
                "Simple CASE compares with `=` only, so it ==never matches NULL=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "SELECT CASE WHEN score >= 90 THEN 'A'",
                "            WHEN score >= 80 THEN 'B'",
                "            ELSE 'C' END,",
                "       CASE status WHEN 'a' THEN 1 END",
                "FROM results;"
              ],
              "note": "searched, then simple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. COALESCE and NULLIF",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Function",
                "Returns",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`COALESCE(a, b, c)`",
                  "first {green:non-NULL} argument",
                  "defaults"
                ],
                [
                  "`NULLIF(a, b)`",
                  "NULL if a = b, else a",
                  "safe division"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "SELECT COALESCE(discount, 0),",
                "       total / NULLIF(qty, 0)",
                "FROM orders;"
              ],
              "note": "qty = 0 gives NULL, not an error"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Gotchas",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "CASE branches must return ==compatible types==",
                "`NULL + 1` is ==NULL==, not 1"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Before arithmetic",
              "text": "Wrap nullable columns: `COALESCE(col, 0) + 1`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "CAST and Numeric Rounding",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "CAST and Numeric Rounding",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. CAST syntax",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`CAST(x AS INTEGER)` is ==standard SQL==",
                "PostgreSQL also accepts `x::integer`",
                "Bad strings and decimals behave differently per engine: ==see the table=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Engine",
                "CAST(2.5 AS INT)",
                "CAST('abc' AS INT)"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "PostgreSQL",
                  "3 (**rounds**)",
                  "error"
                ],
                [
                  "MySQL",
                  "3 (**rounds**), written `AS SIGNED`",
                  "0 + warning"
                ],
                [
                  "SQL Server",
                  "2 (**truncates**)",
                  "error"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Rounding and division",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`ROUND(x, 2)` rounds to 2 decimals",
                "Negative scale works: `ROUND(1234, -2)` = ==1200==",
                "`CEIL` goes up, `FLOOR` goes down",
                "`TRUNC` cuts toward zero",
                "Integer / integer ==truncates== in PostgreSQL and SQL Server: write `7/2.0` or `CAST(7 AS NUMERIC)/2`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Expression",
                "PostgreSQL",
                "MySQL",
                "SQL Server"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`7/2`",
                  "3",
                  "3.5",
                  "3"
                ],
                [
                  "`7/2.0`",
                  "3.5",
                  "3.5",
                  "3.5"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Money and mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Money in ==NUMERIC/DECIMAL==",
                "FLOAT for money: rounding errors accumulate",
                "`ROUND(float, 2)` may fail in PostgreSQL: cast to NUMERIC first"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Integer division and decimal-to-int casts depend on the engine. Use ==NUMERIC== for money, never FLOAT."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Views and Functions",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Views and Functions",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Views",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW v AS SELECT ...;",
                "CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW mv AS SELECT ...;",
                "REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW CONCURRENTLY mv;",
                "DROP VIEW v;"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==View== = saved SELECT: always fresh, slower",
                "==Materialized== = stored rows: fast, stale until REFRESH",
                "CONCURRENTLY needs a unique index; replace keeps column order"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Strings and Dates",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Rule"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`CONCAT(a,b)`",
                  "NULL as empty (MySQL: NULL)"
                ],
                [
                  "`a || b`",
                  "{red:NULL} if any NULL"
                ],
                [
                  "`SUBSTRING(s,1,3)`",
                  "==1-indexed=="
                ],
                [
                  "`TRIM`, `REPLACE`",
                  "clean; replace all"
                ],
                [
                  "`LIKE '%abc'`",
                  "skips index"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`NOW()` timestamp, `CURRENT_DATE` date",
                "`EXTRACT(YEAR FROM ts)`, `DATE_TRUNC('month', ts)`",
                "`ts + INTERVAL '7 days'`",
                "Range: `ts >= '2026-01-01' AND ts < '2026-02-01'`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. NULLs, Casts, Rounding",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Write"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Default",
                  "`COALESCE(discount, 0)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Safe divide",
                  "`x / NULLIF(y, 0)`"
                ],
                [
                  "No ELSE",
                  "CASE gives NULL"
                ],
                [
                  "Cast",
                  "`CAST(x AS INT)` or `x::int`"
                ],
                [
                  "Round",
                  "`ROUND(x,2)`; CEIL up, FLOOR down, TRUNC cuts"
                ],
                [
                  "Division",
                  "PostgreSQL `7/2` = 3, `7/2.0` = 3.5"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Money",
              "text": "Use ==NUMERIC==, never FLOAT"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "In PostgreSQL, what do `CONCAT('a', NULL, 'b')` and `'a' || NULL || 'b'` return?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "CONCAT gives ==ab==, since it treats NULL as empty",
                "|| gives ==NULL==, since any NULL operand nulls the result"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Bug: `WHERE ts BETWEEN '2026-01-01' AND '2026-01-31'` on a timestamp column. What goes wrong?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "'2026-01-31' means midnight, so rows later on Jan 31 are missed",
                "Use `ts >= '2026-01-01' AND ts < '2026-02-01'`"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "With x NULL, what does `CASE x WHEN NULL THEN 'none' ELSE 'has' END` return?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "==has==, because simple CASE compares with =, and NULL = NULL is never true",
                "Use `CASE WHEN x IS NULL THEN 'none' ...`"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
